Since I'm using it for an experiment, the first version is going to be
a same-every-time maze.  (I know, that's against the spirit of
Nethack, but everyone has to make sacrifices in the name of
Science...)  However, I can't yet figure out how to stop it generating
random monsters in addition to the ones I've specifically placed.

 I've figured out how to remove specific objects (e.g. keys,
lockpicks, and credit cards) from the game, but I know that if I try
to remove everything inconvenient manually, I'll miss something, and
Murphy's Law says the game'll generate it when it's least convenient
(e.g. a monster zapping a wand of digging to make a hole in the floor
which the player falls through to some other, uncontrolled, level...)
So ideally I'd like to turn off random monster generation and random
monster-inventory generation for my levels...  Any number I can easily
change to nerf the probability, for example?

At least this level building is starting to get fun, I put together a
training level yesterday with only a few syntax and compilation
errors...  And a newt.  It needed a newt.

I'm hoping to not run the final experiment in Wizard mode, though that
may be a plan B.  (I'm certainly using it for testing, and having a
bit of fun with it as well...)


